es, and thrust reverser actuation systems for turbine engines and nacelles, as well as flight deck controls, actuators, servocontrols, motors, and sensors for aircraft. This segment also provides aftermarket maintenance, repair and overhaul, and other services to commercial airlines, repair facilities, military depots, third party repair shops, and other end users. Its Industrial segment offers actuators, valves, pumps, fuel injection systems, solenoids, ignition systems, control systems, electronics and software, and sensors used on industrial gas turbines, steam turbines, compressors, and reciprocating engines, as well as aftermarket products and related services. The company primarily serves OEMs and equipment packagers. Woodward, Inc. was founded in 1870 and is headquartered in Fort Collins, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles P. Blankenship Jr. | CEO & Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $350K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Woodward, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $18.7B market cap on $3.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $340M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 119% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.1925499571092268},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $13.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-12982177.6},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","31 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to WWD Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Technical_Reactions_to_WWD_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_110426102802_1793806082.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793806082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Woodward (WWD) Stock Could Be 13% Undervalued On Cash Flow","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-wwd/woodward/news/woodward-wwd-stock-could-be-13-undervalued-on-cash-flow","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793162908.176,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Woodward (WWD) Beat Estimates Again in Its Next Earnings Report?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3015156/will-woodward-wwd-beat-estimates-again-in-its-next-earnings-report?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_7-3015156","date":"2026-10-26","timestamp":1793027401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Missed Woodward's Run? What Holders Had To Believe","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-wwd/woodward/news/missed-woodwards-run-what-holders-had-to-believe","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793791225.039,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.374,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Woodward Schedules Fiscal 2026 Fourth Quarter and Full Year Earnings Release and Conference Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/woodward-schedules-fiscal-2026-fou