unded at 14.4% over 3 years, 7.4% over 5 years and 5.8% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 36% of profits supports about 3.7% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 2.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.07 (orders outpacing sales) and a backlog worth 90% of annual revenue.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.2x, 3.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 93%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (34 sales, net $13.0M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.3% (0.9% in buybacks and 0.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 31 consecutive years, raising it 11.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 10,200 employees, each generates about $350K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 6.2% a year.","That works out to $33K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.6M (13x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 119% above its fair value of $145.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 42, gates 15/26)","Revenue grew 7.4%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.6x","Piotroski F-score 7/9","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 119% above fair value of $145","P/E 35.3x vs sector 23.3x","EV/EBITDA 24.5x vs sector 13.3x","P/FCF 55.0x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":["Priced 119% above its fair value of $145"],"need":[],"buy_below":123.01,"vc":{"base":144.72,"base_src":"dcf","bear":97.26,"bull":219.54,"alt_median":62.17,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.3279,"dispersion":0.3906,"level":"L